{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"b9cadc0df22d7285e7f8e17f","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244%40gmail.com/","channels":["linux-i2c"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244%40gmail.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com"},"subject":"[PATCH] i2c: qcom-cci: fix autosuspend cleanup","messages":{"20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com":{"id":"20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com","messageId":"20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com","references":[],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Guangshuo Li","address":"lgs201920130244@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Loic Poulain","address":"loic.poulain@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Robert Foss","address":"rfoss@kernel.org"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Todor Tomov","address":"todor.too@gmail.com"},{"name":"Wolfram Sang","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"Vinod Koul","address":"vkoul@kernel.org"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Guangshuo Li","address":"lgs201920130244@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T09:44:25.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T09:44:25.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH] i2c: qcom-cci: fix autosuspend cleanup","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"cci_probe() calls pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(), but the remove path\ndoes not call the matching pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() before\ndisabling runtime PM."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"If the autosuspend delay is set to a negative value while autosuspend\nis enabled, the runtime PM core increments usage_count to prevent\nruntime suspend. Without undoing the autosuspend setting during\nteardown, this reference is not dropped and usage_count remains\nunbalanced."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Use devm_pm_runtime_set_active_enabled() to manage the runtime PM\nstate. Its managed cleanup disables autosuspend and runtime PM and\nrestores the suspended state on probe failure and driver removal.\nRemove the now redundant manual runtime PM cleanup."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This issue was found by manual code inspection."},{"kind":"code","text":"Fixes: e517526195de (\"i2c: Add Qualcomm CCI I2C driver\")\nCc: stable@vger.kernel.org"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: Guangshuo Li <lgs201920130244@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com:0:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com:0:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[]},"CAFEp6-177whXgFj1uViqg1Gv=68GkqzG_gYqEbV1kX-9UXkSHw@mail.gmail.com":{"id":"CAFEp6-177whXgFj1uViqg1Gv=68GkqzG_gYqEbV1kX-9UXkSHw@mail.gmail.com","messageId":"CAFEp6-177whXgFj1uViqg1Gv=68GkqzG_gYqEbV1kX-9UXkSHw@mail.gmail.com","references":["20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Loic Poulain","address":"loic.poulain@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Guangshuo Li","address":"lgs201920130244@gmail.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Robert Foss","address":"rfoss@kernel.org"},{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Todor Tomov","address":"todor.too@gmail.com"},{"name":"Wolfram Sang","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"Vinod Koul","address":"vkoul@kernel.org"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T13:50:50.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T13:50:50.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH] i2c: qcom-cci: fix autosuspend cleanup","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Wed, Aug 12, 2026 at 11:46 AM Guangshuo Li <lgs201920130244@gmail.com> wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"cci_probe() calls pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(), but the remove path"},{"depth":1,"text":"does not call the matching pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() before"},{"depth":1,"text":"disabling runtime PM."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"If the autosuspend delay is set to a negative value while autosuspend"},{"depth":1,"text":"is enabled, the runtime PM core increments usage_count to prevent"},{"depth":1,"text":"runtime suspend. Without undoing the autosuspend setting during"},{"depth":1,"text":"teardown, this reference is not dropped and usage_count remains"},{"depth":1,"text":"unbalanced."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Use devm_pm_runtime_set_active_enabled() to manage the runtime PM"},{"depth":1,"text":"state. Its managed cleanup disables autosuspend and runtime PM and"},{"depth":1,"text":"restores the suspended state on probe failure and driver removal."},{"depth":1,"text":"Remove the now redundant manual runtime PM cleanup."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This issue was found by manual code inspection."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Fixes: e517526195de (\"i2c: Add Qualcomm CCI I2C driver\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Guangshuo Li <lgs201920130244@gmail.com>"}],"lineCount":21,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Reviewed-by: Loic Poulain <loic.poulain@oss.qualcomm.com>"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c | 11 ++++-------"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index bdeda3979c48..25b6e4e9e3fa 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -595,9 +595,11 @@ static int cci_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"                goto disable_clocks;"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"        pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(dev, MSEC_PER_SEC);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+       ret = devm_pm_runtime_set_active_enabled(dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+       if (ret)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+               goto disable_clocks;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"        pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-       pm_runtime_set_active(dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-       pm_runtime_enable(dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"        for (i = 0; i < cci->data->num_masters; i++) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"                if (!cci->master[i].cci)"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -613,8 +615,6 @@ static int cci_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"        return 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" error_i2c:"},{"depth":1,"text":"-       pm_runtime_disable(dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-       pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"        for (--i ; i >= 0; i--) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"                if (cci->master[i].cci) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -640,9 +640,6 @@ static void cci_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"                        cci_halt(cci, i);"},{"depth":1,"text":"                }"},{"depth":1,"text":"        }"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-       pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-       pm_runtime_set_suspended(&pdev->dev);"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" static const struct cci_data cci_v1_data = {"},{"depth":1,"text":"--"},{"depth":1,"text":"2.43.0"},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":44,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com","parentId":"20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com"}},"rootIds":["20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com"],"childrenByParent":{"20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com":["CAFEp6-177whXgFj1uViqg1Gv=68GkqzG_gYqEbV1kX-9UXkSHw@mail.gmail.com"]},"chronologicalIds":["20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com","CAFEp6-177whXgFj1uViqg1Gv=68GkqzG_gYqEbV1kX-9UXkSHw@mail.gmail.com"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{"patch:20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com:0:0":{"id":"patch:20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com:0:0","messageId":"20260812094425.3515179-1-lgs201920130244@gmail.com","subject":"[PATCH] i2c: qcom-cci: fix autosuspend cleanup","commitMessage":[],"files":[{"oldPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c","newPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c","displayPath":"drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c","status":"modified","hunks":[{"header":"@@ -595,9 +595,11 @@ static int cci_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)","oldStart":595,"oldCount":9,"newStart":595,"newCount":11,"lines":[{"kind":"context","text":"\t\tgoto disable_clocks;","oldLine":595,"newLine":595},{"kind":"context","text":"","oldLine":596,"newLine":596},{"kind":"context","text":"\tpm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(dev, MSEC_PER_SEC);","oldLine":597,"newLine":597},{"kind":"addition","text":"\tret = devm_pm_runtime_set_active_enabled(dev);","newLine":598},{"kind":"addition","text":"\tif (ret)","newLine":599},{"kind":"addition","text":"\t\tgoto disable_clocks;","newL